1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:01,658
What if you could fly?

2
00:00:01,678 --> 00:00:02,922
No wings.

3
00:00:02,942 --> 00:00:04,150
No jetpack.

4
00:00:04,170 --> 00:00:05,080
You just think:

5
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:05,982
up.

6
00:00:06,002 --> 00:00:06,745
And up you go.

7
00:00:08,096 --> 00:00:09,618
Best superpower ever, right?

8
00:00:09,638 --> 00:00:10,428
No traffic,

9
00:00:10,448 --> 00:00:11,027
no tickets,

10
00:00:11,027 --> 00:00:12,348
no airport security.

11
00:00:12,368 --> 00:00:14,068
Well, your body has a

12
00:00:14,068 --> 00:00:14,997
few complaints.

13
00:00:15,017 --> 00:00:15,809
Let's go up there and

14
00:00:15,809 --> 00:00:16,417
hear them,

15
00:00:16,437 --> 00:00:17,097
one by one.

16
00:00:20,098 --> 00:00:21,869
The first few meters are glorious.

17
00:00:21,889 --> 00:00:23,311
Rooftops, treetops,

18
00:00:23,311 --> 00:00:24,943
one very confused neighbor.

19
00:00:24,963 --> 00:00:26,290
Then you hit your first rule.

20
00:00:27,290 --> 00:00:28,440
In the US and Europe,

21
00:00:28,460 --> 00:00:30,013
small drones generally have to

22
00:00:30,013 --> 00:00:32,654
stay below about 120 meters.

23
00:00:32,674 --> 00:00:33,747
You are not a drone.

24
00:00:33,767 --> 00:00:34,841
Legally, you're a very

25
00:00:34,841 --> 00:00:36,648
confusing case.

26
00:00:36,668 --> 00:00:37,907
Let's speed up.

27
00:00:37,927 --> 00:00:40,127
At 100 km/h,

28
00:00:40,147 --> 00:00:41,113
it's like sticking your head

29
00:00:41,113 --> 00:00:41,916
out of a car on

30
00:00:41,916 --> 00:00:42,912
the highway.

31
00:00:42,932 --> 00:00:43,742
At 200 km/h,

32
00:00:43,762 --> 00:00:44,952
skydiver speed,

33
00:00:44,972 --> 00:00:46,281
the wind hits so hard

34
00:00:46,281 --> 00:00:48,470
your eyes won't stop watering.

35
00:00:48,490 --> 00:00:49,677
Fliers, get goggles.

36
00:00:51,028 --> 00:00:52,253
Then a peregrine falcon

37
00:00:52,253 --> 00:00:53,208
overtakes you.

38
00:00:53,228 --> 00:00:53,938
In a dive,

39
00:00:53,958 --> 00:00:56,887
falcons can top 300 km/h.

40
00:00:56,907 --> 00:00:57,406
Rude.

41
00:00:58,756 --> 00:00:59,999
Want to go faster?

42
00:01:00,019 --> 00:01:02,001
Strike the superhero pose.

43
00:01:02,021 --> 00:01:03,787
Skydivers who fall belly-first

44
00:01:03,787 --> 00:01:05,461
hit about two hundred,

45
00:01:05,481 --> 00:01:05,921
but head-first,

46
00:01:05,941 --> 00:01:07,268
with less air in the

47
00:01:07,268 --> 00:01:08,861
way, many reach around

48
00:01:08,861 --> 00:01:10,538
250 km/h or more.

49
00:01:10,558 --> 00:01:11,098
Less drag,

50
00:01:11,118 --> 00:01:12,295
more speed.

51
00:01:12,315 --> 00:01:13,287
The cape is optional.

52
00:01:14,637 --> 00:01:15,839
Now take a tight turn

53
00:01:15,839 --> 00:01:17,727
at 300 km/h,

54
00:01:17,747 --> 00:01:18,753
on a curve a hundred

55
00:01:18,753 --> 00:01:19,936
meters across.

56
00:01:19,956 --> 00:01:21,123
That squeezes you with around

57
00:01:21,123 --> 00:01:21,726
seven g,

58
00:01:21,746 --> 00:01:23,359
seven times your body weight.

59
00:01:23,379 --> 00:01:25,429
Without training or a g-suit,

60
00:01:25,449 --> 00:01:26,611
many people black out

61
00:01:26,611 --> 00:01:28,683
somewhere between four and six g.

62
00:01:28,703 --> 00:01:30,280
First your vision goes gray.

63
00:01:30,300 --> 00:01:30,929
Then black.

64
00:01:32,278 --> 00:01:34,364
Air cools by about 6.5 degrees

65
00:01:34,364 --> 00:01:35,858
Celsius for every kilometer

66
00:01:35,858 --> 00:01:36,999
you climb.

67
00:01:37,019 --> 00:01:38,319
So on a warm day,

68
00:01:38,339 --> 00:01:39,349
three kilometers up it's

69
00:01:39,349 --> 00:01:40,597
already around freezing.

70
00:01:40,617 --> 00:01:41,527
Add the wind:

71
00:01:41,547 --> 00:01:42,757
at minus twenty,

72
00:01:42,777 --> 00:01:45,167
flying at 100 km/h,

73
00:01:45,187 --> 00:01:47,163
it feels like minus forty.

74
00:01:47,183 --> 00:01:48,727
Exposed skin can get frostbite

75
00:01:48,727 --> 00:01:49,822
in around ten minutes.

76
00:01:50,822 --> 00:01:52,093
Climb fast and your ears

77
00:01:52,093 --> 00:01:53,227
start to hurt.

78
00:01:53,247 --> 00:01:54,211
Air trapped behind your

79
00:01:54,211 --> 00:01:55,380
eardrums can't keep up with

80
00:01:55,380 --> 00:01:56,397
the pressure change,

81
00:01:56,417 --> 00:01:57,567
just like on a plane,

82
00:01:57,587 --> 00:01:58,446
only faster.

83
00:01:58,466 --> 00:01:59,574
Swallow, yawn,

84
00:01:59,574 --> 00:02:02,260
and wait for that satisfying pop.

85
00:02:02,280 --> 00:02:03,298
And clouds?

86
00:02:03,318 --> 00:02:04,918
They look like cotton candy,

87
00:02:04,938 --> 00:02:06,050
but they're made of billions

88
00:02:06,050 --> 00:02:07,399
of tiny water droplets.

89
00:02:07,419 --> 00:02:08,435
Fly through one and you

90
00:02:08,435 --> 00:02:09,375
come out soaked.

91
00:02:09,395 --> 00:02:10,155
In the cold,

92
00:02:10,175 --> 00:02:11,525
those droplets can freeze onto

93
00:02:11,525 --> 00:02:12,034
you as ice.

94
00:02:13,035 --> 00:02:14,196
Keep climbing and the air

95
00:02:14,196 --> 00:02:14,946
gets thin.

96
00:02:14,966 --> 00:02:16,456
Above about three kilometers,

97
00:02:16,476 --> 00:02:18,076
low oxygen starts messing with

98
00:02:18,076 --> 00:02:19,002
your judgment.

99
00:02:19,022 --> 00:02:19,925
At the top of Mount

100
00:02:19,925 --> 00:02:21,774
Everest, there's only about a

101
00:02:21,774 --> 00:02:22,816
third of the air pressure

102
00:02:22,816 --> 00:02:24,201
you'd have at sea level.

103
00:02:24,221 --> 00:02:25,433
Climbers spend weeks letting

104
00:02:25,433 --> 00:02:26,846
their bodies adapt to that.

105
00:02:26,866 --> 00:02:28,948
You'd get there in minutes.

106
00:02:28,968 --> 00:02:30,188
Now try plane height,

107
00:02:30,208 --> 00:02:31,978
about 10 kilometers up.

108
00:02:31,998 --> 00:02:34,178
It's around minus fifty outside.

109
00:02:34,198 --> 00:02:35,586
Airliners keep their cabins at

110
00:02:35,586 --> 00:02:36,498
the pressure of about

111
00:02:36,498 --> 00:02:38,878
2,400 meters, but you don't

112
00:02:38,878 --> 00:02:39,987
have a cabin.

113
00:02:40,007 --> 00:02:40,967
At that height,

114
00:02:40,987 --> 00:02:42,411
people who lose cabin pressure

115
00:02:42,411 --> 00:02:43,756
have roughly 30 to 60

116
00:02:43,756 --> 00:02:45,770
seconds of useful consciousness.

117
00:02:45,790 --> 00:02:47,312
After that, you're not flying.

118
00:02:47,332 --> 00:02:47,916
You're falling.

119
00:02:49,266 --> 00:02:50,276
Fun fact:

120
00:02:50,296 --> 00:02:51,579
the highest-flying bird ever

121
00:02:51,579 --> 00:02:53,626
recorded, a Rüppell's vulture,

122
00:02:53,646 --> 00:02:55,070
hit an airliner at about

123
00:02:55,070 --> 00:02:57,871
11,300 meters over West Africa

124
00:02:57,871 --> 00:03:00,227
in 1973.

125
00:03:00,247 --> 00:03:01,202
It did not end well

126
00:03:01,202 --> 00:03:01,868
for the vulture.

127
00:03:02,869 --> 00:03:04,362
Bonus problems.

128
00:03:04,382 --> 00:03:06,097
UV radiation gets about ten

129
00:03:06,097 --> 00:03:07,280
percent stronger for every

130
00:03:07,280 --> 00:03:08,842
thousand meters you climb,

131
00:03:08,862 --> 00:03:10,613
so sunscreen is mandatory.

132
00:03:10,633 --> 00:03:12,599
And never fly into a thunderstorm.

133
00:03:12,619 --> 00:03:14,430
Updrafts inside big storms can

134
00:03:14,430 --> 00:03:16,889
top 150 km/h,

135
00:03:16,909 --> 00:03:18,236
with hail and lightning on

136
00:03:18,236 --> 00:03:18,730
the side.

137
00:03:20,080 --> 00:03:21,603
So here's your flight checklist.

138
00:03:21,623 --> 00:03:22,707
Goggles.

139
00:03:22,727 --> 00:03:24,338
A ski jacket and gloves.

140
00:03:24,358 --> 00:03:26,430
Stay below three kilometers.

141
00:03:26,450 --> 00:03:26,980
Make wide,

142
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:28,267
gentle turns.

143
00:03:28,287 --> 00:03:29,706
Wear sunscreen.

144
00:03:29,726 --> 00:03:31,097
And stay far away from

145
00:03:31,097 --> 00:03:32,501
storms and airports.

146
00:03:32,521 --> 00:03:34,315
Basically: dress like a skier,

147
00:03:34,315 --> 00:03:36,724
and fly like a nervous pigeon.

148
00:03:36,744 --> 00:03:38,044
Real humans have tried,

149
00:03:38,064 --> 00:03:38,975
the hard way.

150
00:03:38,995 --> 00:03:40,645
In 1988,

151
00:03:40,665 --> 00:03:42,054
Greek cyclist Kanellos

152
00:03:42,054 --> 00:03:43,443
Kanellopoulos pedaled a

153
00:03:43,443 --> 00:03:44,741
feather-light aircraft called

154
00:03:44,741 --> 00:03:47,087
Daedalus 115 kilometers across

155
00:03:47,087 --> 00:03:48,335
the Aegean Sea,

156
00:03:48,355 --> 00:03:50,295
in just under four hours.

157
00:03:50,315 --> 00:03:52,185
That's almost three marathons,

158
00:03:52,205 --> 00:03:52,995
in the air,

159
00:03:53,015 --> 00:03:54,311
powered only by his legs.

160
00:03:55,311 --> 00:03:56,913
So, could you handle flying?

161
00:03:56,933 --> 00:03:58,261
With the right gear, a little.

162
00:03:58,281 --> 00:03:58,742
Without it,

163
00:03:58,742 --> 00:03:59,787
your body would quit long

164
00:03:59,787 --> 00:04:01,140
before your superpower does.

165
00:04:01,160 --> 00:04:01,889
Wait...

166
00:04:01,909 --> 00:04:02,328
Newton?

167
00:04:04,529 --> 00:04:05,605
Next time on What If

168
00:04:05,605 --> 00:04:07,287
Bix: what if everyone on

169
00:04:07,287 --> 00:04:08,452
Earth jumped at the exact

170
00:04:08,452 --> 00:04:09,124
same moment?

171
00:04:10,523 --> 00:04:12,135
Thanks for flying with Bix.

172
00:04:12,155 --> 00:04:13,253
Please keep your seatbelt

173
00:04:13,253 --> 00:04:14,597
fastened until the video comes

174
00:04:14,597 --> 00:04:15,877
to a complete stop.

175
00:04:15,897 --> 00:04:16,952
Watch another what if right

176
00:04:16,952 --> 00:04:18,185
here, and subscribe,

177
00:04:18,185 --> 00:04:19,329
so Newton has company.
